WEBVTT

00:00:12.950 --> 00:00:16.490
Polar Bear's Café

00:01:29.980 --> 00:01:34.940
Polar 
Bear's 
Café

00:01:31.950 --> 00:01:34.300
Christmas Planning!

00:01:48.850 --> 00:01:50.370
The cold invades.

00:01:50.880 --> 00:01:52.890
Charley horse.

00:01:54.060 --> 00:01:56.760
Exercise with caution.

00:02:02.640 --> 00:02:03.800
Goodness.

00:02:03.800 --> 00:02:06.260
Lazing around all day 
yesterday and today.

00:02:06.660 --> 00:02:07.720
What?

00:02:08.270 --> 00:02:12.780
Yesterday I was laying 
around, not lazing around.

00:02:13.110 --> 00:02:16.350
<i>Even though we're small</i>

00:02:14.180 --> 00:02:15.860
<i>To the people we need to thank</i>

00:02:16.270 --> 00:02:18.580
Oh, it's Yama Arashi!

00:02:16.670 --> 00:02:19.090
<i>We're unstoppable!</i>

00:02:19.020 --> 00:02:20.320
<i>A Christmas present...</i>

00:02:19.620 --> 00:02:22.410
<i>Drum with our feet</i>

00:02:20.890 --> 00:02:22.410
<i>...from the bottom of our hearts!</i>

00:02:22.930 --> 00:02:26.060
Yama Arashi are so cool.

00:02:26.870 --> 00:02:28.910
I want a present.

00:02:29.200 --> 00:02:30.690
Mom,

00:02:31.200 --> 00:02:34.880
I've been so nice to you
that you should get me a present.

00:02:34.880 --> 00:02:38.000
All you do is clean, after all.

00:02:41.980 --> 00:02:44.850
Don't suck me up!

00:02:44.850 --> 00:02:49.850
Polar 
Bear's 
Café

00:02:50.160 --> 00:02:53.970
I really do need to get a present.

00:02:53.970 --> 00:02:55.360
What?

00:02:55.360 --> 00:02:56.930
What are you going to get me?

00:02:56.930 --> 00:03:01.850
It's not for <i>you</i>. It's for Prince Han.

00:03:01.850 --> 00:03:04.070
I wonder what I should get.

00:03:04.570 --> 00:03:06.790
If it's for Mr. Handa, 
you should get him a brush.

00:03:07.250 --> 00:03:09.500
Huh? Why a brush?

00:03:09.840 --> 00:03:12.800
Mr. Handa really likes 
to clean his bathroom,

00:03:13.230 --> 00:03:16.300
so he'll remember you 
every time he uses it.

00:03:16.700 --> 00:03:19.470
What? But that's so boring.

00:03:19.750 --> 00:03:22.610
Mr. Handa said that his 
dream is to live in

00:03:22.610 --> 00:03:24.140
a house with ten bathtubs.

00:03:24.140 --> 00:03:25.880
What? Really?

00:03:25.880 --> 00:03:27.640
Does he really want to clean that much?

00:03:28.320 --> 00:03:30.800
At least that's how I imagine him.

00:03:31.350 --> 00:03:33.650
I was an idiot to believe 
you even for a second.

00:03:34.340 --> 00:03:36.770
I think I'll just give him my picture.

00:03:37.240 --> 00:03:39.490
That way we'll always be together.

00:03:41.240 --> 00:03:44.780
What? I don't think he'll want that.

00:03:45.160 --> 00:03:46.770
That's not true!

00:03:47.450 --> 00:03:49.920
You should give him my picture.

00:03:49.920 --> 00:03:52.470
My picture is better!

00:03:52.470 --> 00:03:54.600
He'll totally say I'm cute!

00:03:54.600 --> 00:03:55.430
Bleh!

00:03:56.090 --> 00:03:58.830
He'll say that I'm cuter!

00:03:59.430 --> 00:04:00.540
Both of you...

00:04:01.460 --> 00:04:02.820
If you're going to fight about it,

00:04:02.820 --> 00:04:04.720
just send him a picture of me.

00:04:05.260 --> 00:04:09.680
What? But you're not cute, Mom.

00:04:15.290 --> 00:04:18.110
Don't suck me up!

00:04:20.820 --> 00:04:24.030
I wonder if there's anyone 
who'll give me a present.

00:04:24.950 --> 00:04:27.920
Like maybe a new panda pochette.

00:04:33.290 --> 00:04:36.520
I'd like a fluffy, hand-knitted one.

00:04:43.920 --> 00:04:45.500
Hello!

00:04:46.280 --> 00:04:47.340
Welcome.

00:04:47.760 --> 00:04:49.300
Hey, Panda.

00:04:50.590 --> 00:04:51.220
Huh?

00:04:51.980 --> 00:04:55.520
I've never seen you dress
 like that, Polar Bear.

00:04:56.040 --> 00:04:59.230
I mixed things up for Christmas.

00:04:59.500 --> 00:05:01.230
So cool!

00:05:01.920 --> 00:05:06.940
I wonder if I'll look cooler 
if I get a new pochette.

00:05:06.940 --> 00:05:08.770
<i>You're wonderful, Mr. Panda!</i>

00:05:08.770 --> 00:05:10.680
<i>So cool and cute!</i>

00:05:10.680 --> 00:05:12.120
<i>So cooly cute!</i>

00:05:13.030 --> 00:05:16.240
I don't think a pochette 
wields that much power.

00:05:16.920 --> 00:05:19.590
Well, if it isn't Panda.

00:05:20.280 --> 00:05:22.770
Huh? A pretty Mr. Llama?

00:05:23.550 --> 00:05:24.990
I'm right here.

00:05:26.000 --> 00:05:29.300
Hello, nice to meet you. 
My name is Alpaca.

00:05:30.120 --> 00:05:31.640
What are you doing?

00:05:32.230 --> 00:05:34.030
We're preparing for Christmas.

00:05:34.430 --> 00:05:35.270
Preparing?

00:05:36.200 --> 00:05:37.960
Every year for Christmas,

00:05:37.960 --> 00:05:40.240
Mr. Alpaca and I use our wool

00:05:40.240 --> 00:05:42.290
to make hand-knitted items.

00:05:43.330 --> 00:05:45.350
We have to send them to many places

00:05:45.350 --> 00:05:46.700
so we're a little panicked.

00:05:47.400 --> 00:05:50.120
Wow, they're so cute.

00:05:50.800 --> 00:05:55.620
Our yarn and our felt is 
quite popular every year.

00:05:56.020 --> 00:06:00.540
Everyone worries when they see 
us without our coats every year.

00:06:00.540 --> 00:06:03.880
Oh, so when you lost all that weight,

00:06:03.880 --> 00:06:05.590
it was just because your coat was gone.

00:06:05.880 --> 00:06:09.150
Yes. We make yarn with it and dye it,

00:06:09.150 --> 00:06:10.720
so it's a lot of work...

00:06:11.240 --> 00:06:13.110
It makes everyone happy,

00:06:13.110 --> 00:06:14.970
so that keeps us going year after year.

00:06:15.490 --> 00:06:17.230
That's nice.

00:06:17.740 --> 00:06:22.940
Could you make a panda 
pochette with alpaca wool?

00:06:23.170 --> 00:06:25.900
What? Not llama wool?

00:06:26.120 --> 00:06:30.260
Well, alpaca wool
 seems more luxurious.

00:06:33.990 --> 00:06:35.020
So,

00:06:35.020 --> 00:06:38.360
how are you going to spend 
your Christmas, Miss Sasako?

00:06:38.970 --> 00:06:43.500
We'll be serving a special 
 Christmas dinner.

00:06:43.830 --> 00:06:45.500
It's a great time to make a profit.

00:06:45.860 --> 00:06:47.430
Cha-ching!

00:06:48.180 --> 00:06:51.220
Could you not put it 
so bluntly like that?

00:06:51.800 --> 00:06:55.180
What are you personally
going to do for Christmas?

00:06:55.690 --> 00:06:57.890
I'll be serving customers
 and washing dishes.

00:06:58.180 --> 00:07:00.850
No, I mean after work.

00:07:01.250 --> 00:07:02.310
I'll go home.

00:07:04.320 --> 00:07:06.140
There is something else, right?

00:07:06.140 --> 00:07:08.010
Like in between work and going home?

00:07:08.260 --> 00:07:09.110
Oh!

00:07:09.470 --> 00:07:10.400
Yeah, that.

00:07:10.910 --> 00:07:12.940
I have to stop at the grocery store

00:07:12.940 --> 00:07:15.740
and buy some thick Aegean Sea yogurt.

00:07:18.510 --> 00:07:20.760
Really? Yogurt for Christmas?

00:07:20.760 --> 00:07:22.540
Exactly how much do you like that stuff?

00:07:22.540 --> 00:07:25.140
It's delicious. I highly recommend it.

00:07:25.610 --> 00:07:28.190
It's not the matter of it 
being delicious or not!

00:07:28.190 --> 00:07:31.530
None of you are putting enough 
thought into Christmas!

00:07:32.680 --> 00:07:35.220
What did you have in mind, Mr. Penguin?

00:07:35.750 --> 00:07:41.520
You have to handle seasonal events 
like Christmas properly.

00:07:41.520 --> 00:07:43.560
Like putting up a Christmas tree,

00:07:43.560 --> 00:07:47.440
eating cake, and exchanging presents.

00:07:48.910 --> 00:07:51.320
That's what Christmas is all about.

00:07:51.670 --> 00:07:53.570
You came prepared?

00:07:54.080 --> 00:07:56.030
I have enough for everyone, too.

00:07:56.610 --> 00:08:00.830
Let's all get together, 
throw a party, and have fun!

00:08:01.320 --> 00:08:02.840
Get together and have fun?

00:08:03.170 --> 00:08:04.250
Yeah.

00:08:04.940 --> 00:08:07.460
Maybe you should get on 
a crowded train, then.

00:08:07.910 --> 00:08:08.840
That's not it.

00:08:09.330 --> 00:08:11.880
How about crossing a 
huge intersection?

00:08:12.360 --> 00:08:13.830
No!

00:08:13.830 --> 00:08:15.780
I don't mean getting together like that.

00:08:15.780 --> 00:08:17.600
I mean something a little 
more fun <i>(wai wai)</i>.

00:08:19.400 --> 00:08:20.810
Oh, you mean like a festival.

00:08:21.260 --> 00:08:22.910
No, that would be heave-ho <i>(wasshoi)</i>.

00:08:22.910 --> 00:08:24.060
That's not it!

00:08:24.400 --> 00:08:26.210
I'm saying we should have a party!

00:08:26.210 --> 00:08:28.320
It can even be after you 
close up the shop.

00:08:28.890 --> 00:08:30.420
You'll come right, Panda?

00:08:30.820 --> 00:08:32.790
I'll even do some of my traditional 
comedic story-telling.

00:08:34.690 --> 00:08:37.740
Could I answer at the 
absolute last minute?

00:08:38.110 --> 00:08:40.090
Or I could do that right now.

00:08:41.170 --> 00:08:45.260
Well, let's start off with 
a slightly idiotic tale.

00:08:45.260 --> 00:08:47.420
It's starting to get 
chilly again this year.

00:08:47.940 --> 00:08:49.630
And now for our next speaker.

00:08:50.590 --> 00:08:52.170
I wasn't done!

00:08:52.810 --> 00:08:53.890
Oh, well.

00:08:54.590 --> 00:08:57.460
What are you two going to do, 
Mr. Llama and Mr. Alpaca?

00:08:57.460 --> 00:08:59.050
Do you two have plans?

00:08:59.690 --> 00:09:03.600
I'm sorry, but we go 
to mass each year.

00:09:07.270 --> 00:09:09.060
You guys are really traditional, huh?

00:09:11.930 --> 00:09:13.250
Hello.

00:09:13.870 --> 00:09:16.450
I came to deliver your 
Christmas wreath.

00:09:16.870 --> 00:09:18.740
Oh, it's so pretty!

00:09:18.740 --> 00:09:20.910
You're amazing, Mr. Rin Rin!

00:09:21.310 --> 00:09:24.160
Don't I know it?

00:09:24.700 --> 00:09:29.360
I got all excited thinking about 
Panda seeing my wreath.

00:09:30.530 --> 00:09:31.840
What's wrong?

00:09:32.380 --> 00:09:34.090
Oh, nothing much...

00:09:34.540 --> 00:09:38.500
Speaking of Christmas, 
I've already ordered my cake.

00:09:39.220 --> 00:09:41.350
It's a cake in the shape of a panda.

00:09:41.980 --> 00:09:43.930
So your cake is a panda, as well?

00:09:44.500 --> 00:09:46.090
That's not all!

00:09:46.860 --> 00:09:49.310
My Christmas cards are 
also panda shaped.

00:09:49.310 --> 00:09:52.050
Not to mention a panda tree, 
and a panda Santa.

00:09:52.580 --> 00:09:54.410
And in preparation for next 
year, a panda calender,

00:09:54.410 --> 00:09:56.100
panda New Year's cards, 
a panda decorative pine tree,

00:09:56.100 --> 00:09:58.490
panda New Year's food, and 
panda New Year's soup!

00:09:59.560 --> 00:10:00.930
Wow, that's amazing.

00:10:00.930 --> 00:10:03.270
I wasn't aware that 
the world was filled

00:10:03.270 --> 00:10:04.720
with that many panda goods.

00:10:05.870 --> 00:10:08.700
You didn't mention any panda lights!

00:10:09.320 --> 00:10:11.660
Oh, I didn't know you 
were here, Panda!

00:10:13.010 --> 00:10:14.670
He found me...

00:10:14.670 --> 00:10:18.630
Polar
Bear's 
Café

00:10:19.220 --> 00:10:20.350
So...

00:10:20.840 --> 00:10:24.560
I'll be sending you a 
Christmas present, Panda!

00:10:25.340 --> 00:10:27.750
I don't want it.

00:10:28.230 --> 00:10:29.060
Oh, I know.

00:10:29.680 --> 00:10:32.330
How about the panda  
wood carving I found online?

00:10:32.920 --> 00:10:34.570
I don't really want it.

00:10:35.420 --> 00:10:37.490
How about a panda matryoshka doll?

00:10:38.100 --> 00:10:39.450
I already have one.

00:10:40.180 --> 00:10:41.950
How about a panda hug pillow?

00:10:42.310 --> 00:10:44.200
I won't use something like that!

00:10:45.970 --> 00:10:48.390
I wonder what you'd like.

00:10:48.800 --> 00:10:51.130
I told you, I don't want anything!

00:10:52.160 --> 00:10:55.520
<i>Rin Rin would never figure 
out what I want!</i>

00:10:55.960 --> 00:10:57.940
<i>Our tastes are completely different.</i>

00:10:57.940 --> 00:11:03.050
<i>The thing I want most right 
now is a panda pochette!</i>

00:11:03.720 --> 00:11:06.770
Then I'll think about 
it until Christmas.

00:11:07.540 --> 00:11:08.600
<i>Just kidding.</i>

00:11:08.600 --> 00:11:10.550
<i>I already know what 
I'm going to give you.</i>

00:11:13.570 --> 00:11:15.790
<i>I'm knitting it right now,</i>

00:11:15.790 --> 00:11:17.400
<i>putting love into every stitch.</i>

00:11:18.040 --> 00:11:19.860
<i>A hand-knitted panda pouch!</i>

00:11:20.780 --> 00:11:22.510
<i>You can even use it as a pochette,</i>

00:11:23.850 --> 00:11:25.280
<i>and we'll be matching.</i>

00:11:26.500 --> 00:11:28.500
<i>I hope Panda will like it!</i>

00:11:31.420 --> 00:11:41.970
Polar 
Bear's 
Café

00:11:41.970 --> 00:11:46.930
Polar 
Bear's 
Café

00:11:43.530 --> 00:11:45.740
Christmas Trouble!

00:11:50.500 --> 00:11:51.780
Thanks for your hard work.

00:11:52.450 --> 00:11:54.100
Thank you!

00:11:54.500 --> 00:11:55.890
Miss Sasako.

00:11:55.890 --> 00:11:56.750
Yes?

00:11:57.280 --> 00:11:59.920
Didn't you forget to 
say something to me?

00:12:02.350 --> 00:12:04.160
I mean, are you sure

00:12:04.530 --> 00:12:07.240
you don't need to invite 
me to a party or something?

00:12:07.980 --> 00:12:09.290
I'm sure.

00:12:10.160 --> 00:12:11.440
Oh, I see.

00:12:12.000 --> 00:12:13.010
Goodnight, then.

00:12:13.550 --> 00:12:14.860
Goodnight!

00:12:21.180 --> 00:12:22.760
How odd.

00:12:23.130 --> 00:12:25.990
Tomorrow's Christmas Eve,

00:12:25.990 --> 00:12:28.990
but no one's invited me to a party.

00:12:29.510 --> 00:12:32.180
And I've been practicing my traditional 
comedic story-telling, too.

00:12:32.460 --> 00:12:33.900
Mr. Penguin.

00:12:33.900 --> 00:12:36.690
If you're free, do you want to 
stop by Grizzly's Bar for a bit?

00:12:40.320 --> 00:12:44.070
Welcome. Good evening!

00:12:44.350 --> 00:12:47.030
Oh? Where's Grizzly?

00:12:47.520 --> 00:12:48.670
During the winter,

00:12:48.670 --> 00:12:53.000
Mr. Grizzly asks me to 
help out at the bar.

00:12:53.510 --> 00:12:54.610
I see.

00:12:59.000 --> 00:13:01.970
Mr. Penguin, if you're 
free tomorrow...

00:13:01.970 --> 00:13:03.880
Huh? What? Are you having a party?

00:13:04.520 --> 00:13:06.340
Why don't you do some major cleaning?

00:13:06.690 --> 00:13:07.840
No way!

00:13:07.840 --> 00:13:10.060
There's no way I'd do 
something so productive!

00:13:10.060 --> 00:13:13.840
Pardon me, Mr. Penguin, 
are you free tomorrow?

00:13:13.840 --> 00:13:15.420
Ooh, are you having a party?

00:13:15.890 --> 00:13:20.440
No... I was wondering if you'd 
take my shift tomorrow night.

00:13:21.310 --> 00:13:24.820
Why am I being asked to 
work a part-time shift?

00:13:25.340 --> 00:13:26.590
What am I going to do?

00:13:26.590 --> 00:13:28.480
I have a date with my girlfriend...

00:13:28.480 --> 00:13:32.420
Then why don't you have her 
come down to Grizzly's Bar?

00:13:32.420 --> 00:13:33.650
You could have some drinks together.

00:13:33.650 --> 00:13:35.390
No!

00:13:35.390 --> 00:13:38.210
I'd like to spend some 
time alone with her.

00:13:38.630 --> 00:13:40.810
What am I going to do, Polar Bear?

00:13:40.810 --> 00:13:42.480
At this rate, 
I won't be able to present

00:13:42.480 --> 00:13:44.840
my traditional comedic 
story-telling anywhere.

00:13:44.840 --> 00:13:47.440
I think that may be 
okay in its own way.

00:13:48.050 --> 00:13:49.750
I'll do it now, then!

00:13:49.750 --> 00:13:51.690
Check please, Otter.

00:13:56.040 --> 00:13:57.830
Daily pad calender renewal.

00:13:57.830 --> 00:14:00.440
Today is a holiday.

00:14:01.120 --> 00:14:03.150
All aboard!

00:14:04.150 --> 00:14:05.630
...Aboard.

00:14:09.080 --> 00:14:11.370
Today is finally the day...

00:14:11.860 --> 00:14:13.360
What do you mean?

00:14:13.360 --> 00:14:15.130
Christmas Eve.

00:14:15.130 --> 00:14:17.140
Oh, you're right.

00:14:17.140 --> 00:14:18.850
Today will be very busy.

00:14:19.400 --> 00:14:21.380
We can't let our guard down.

00:14:21.380 --> 00:14:22.380
What do you mean?

00:14:22.940 --> 00:14:26.860
There's no telling when or who 
I'll be getting presents from today.

00:14:27.260 --> 00:14:29.530
You must lead a very happy life.

00:14:29.530 --> 00:14:30.870
Now, now.

00:14:33.550 --> 00:14:35.060
I didn't order this.

00:14:35.460 --> 00:14:37.480
It's a Christmas present.

00:14:39.900 --> 00:14:42.380
Really? Thank you.

00:14:42.720 --> 00:14:48.730
Oh... But since we weren't 
expecting a gift from you,

00:14:48.730 --> 00:14:53.030
we didn't bring anything 
in return, right, Panda?

00:14:54.100 --> 00:14:56.980
I'll repay you with my cuteness.

00:15:00.450 --> 00:15:03.340
Well, I guess that works...

00:15:03.870 --> 00:15:05.140
Don't worry about it.

00:15:05.650 --> 00:15:08.290
It's the thought that counts.

00:15:10.950 --> 00:15:13.910
You're so cool, Polar Bear.

00:15:21.230 --> 00:15:22.810
Hibernating

00:15:24.080 --> 00:15:25.360
What?!

00:15:25.360 --> 00:15:27.150
It says right here that I'm 
hibernating, doesn't it?!

00:15:29.080 --> 00:15:31.380
I-I-I have a package for you...

00:15:32.080 --> 00:15:34.290
Oh, sorry.

00:15:34.290 --> 00:15:36.730
I thought Polar Bear was 
messing around again.

00:15:37.310 --> 00:15:38.400
Thank ya.

00:15:38.990 --> 00:15:40.590
I'll be going now.

00:15:42.170 --> 00:15:45.130
Polar Bear

00:15:48.440 --> 00:15:50.050
Hello. This is Polar Bear's Ca—

00:15:50.050 --> 00:15:52.800
What the hell are you trying 
to do, you bastard?!

00:15:53.220 --> 00:15:56.280
I told you I'd be hibernating!

00:15:56.280 --> 00:15:59.040
Not to mention, why the hell did 
you send me vegetable oil?!

00:15:56.970 --> 00:16:00.180
Healthy Vegetable 
Oil Light

00:15:56.970 --> 00:16:00.180
Healthy Vegetable 
Oil

00:15:56.970 --> 00:16:00.180
Lowers 
Cholesterol

00:15:59.040 --> 00:16:00.180
That's a year-end gift!

00:16:02.440 --> 00:16:04.250
I think that was somewhat a success.

00:16:04.660 --> 00:16:06.400
How do you figure?

00:16:06.930 --> 00:16:10.770
Oh, that's right. 
There's a gift for you, Panda.

00:16:11.500 --> 00:16:13.710
Really? What is it?

00:16:14.180 --> 00:16:16.410
Bamboo grass? Bamboo shoots?

00:16:18.030 --> 00:16:21.080
A panda pochette! It's so fluffy!

00:16:21.650 --> 00:16:24.330
Thank you so much, Miss Sasako!

00:16:24.650 --> 00:16:26.450
It's not from me...

00:16:26.850 --> 00:16:27.560
Huh?

00:16:32.990 --> 00:16:35.140
Nice smile, Panda!

00:16:35.140 --> 00:16:37.230
I knew you'd like it!

00:16:37.230 --> 00:16:42.180
Th-This is from you, Rin Rin?

00:16:42.620 --> 00:16:43.520
It is!

00:16:45.120 --> 00:16:47.110
I... I don't want it...

00:16:47.590 --> 00:16:50.070
It'll look great on you, Panda!

00:16:53.580 --> 00:16:56.440
O-Of course it will!

00:16:56.440 --> 00:16:58.740
There's no reason it wouldn't!

00:16:59.270 --> 00:17:01.270
Next stop, the end of the line.

00:17:01.270 --> 00:17:03.290
End of the line.

00:17:03.290 --> 00:17:05.310
Please be sure to take

00:17:05.310 --> 00:17:07.560
all of your belongings with you.

00:17:08.160 --> 00:17:10.710
Please be sure...

00:17:13.680 --> 00:17:14.930
Thanks for your hard work.

00:17:15.510 --> 00:17:17.140
Thank you!

00:17:17.600 --> 00:17:19.680
Miss Sasako, Miss Sasako.

00:17:19.680 --> 00:17:20.670
Yes?

00:17:20.670 --> 00:17:23.930
Are you really just buying 
yogurt and heading home?

00:17:24.430 --> 00:17:27.150
Indeed. See you tomorrow.

00:17:31.280 --> 00:17:33.910
Do you want to go out for 
a drink, Polar Bear?

00:17:34.330 --> 00:17:37.180
Sorry, I have some plans.

00:17:37.180 --> 00:17:38.620
What?!

00:17:40.440 --> 00:17:41.990
Could I get another?

00:17:43.080 --> 00:17:43.880
Sure.

00:17:44.780 --> 00:17:47.080
So this is what you meant by plans?

00:17:47.500 --> 00:17:48.360
Yup. Part-time job.

00:17:48.870 --> 00:17:52.460
Could it be that you took 
the shift for Otter?

00:17:53.120 --> 00:17:54.470
<i>Cheers!</i>

00:17:54.820 --> 00:17:58.610
Nah. I just wanted to use a shaker.

00:18:00.660 --> 00:18:02.140
So cool.

00:18:02.640 --> 00:18:05.130
Mr. Polar Bear, could I get another?

00:18:05.620 --> 00:18:06.350
Sure.

00:18:07.140 --> 00:18:09.060
Are you by yourself today?

00:18:09.410 --> 00:18:13.280
Yeah. Tiger is with his family 
and Wolf has his part-time job.

00:18:13.730 --> 00:18:15.320
Merry Xmas!

00:18:16.030 --> 00:18:17.280
Welcome.

00:18:17.280 --> 00:18:19.740
Polar 
Bear's 
Café

00:18:20.640 --> 00:18:23.420
We have lost the Christmas 
sales battle.

00:18:26.800 --> 00:18:27.990
Why?!

00:18:27.990 --> 00:18:32.330
Penguin cards are 
the perfect Christmas gift.

00:18:32.330 --> 00:18:34.090
And yet...

00:18:34.090 --> 00:18:35.250
Don't cry.

00:18:35.250 --> 00:18:37.490
There are just too many 
people in the world

00:18:37.490 --> 00:18:38.720
that just don't understand.

00:18:39.540 --> 00:18:41.220
I'm guessing they didn't sell.

00:18:44.870 --> 00:18:47.430
There are two sets packaged together.

00:18:47.430 --> 00:18:49.140
One red, one green.

00:18:49.510 --> 00:18:52.650
We even wrapped them 
to fit the season.

00:18:53.530 --> 00:18:56.070
We prepared so well, and yet...

00:18:56.070 --> 00:18:58.530
Returned Goods

00:18:56.530 --> 00:18:59.070
We now have a mountain 
of returned goods!

00:18:59.070 --> 00:19:03.280
I was hoping people would enjoy 
playing with them at Christmas parties.

00:19:04.090 --> 00:19:06.010
You're not the only ones bummed out.

00:19:06.010 --> 00:19:09.000
I wanted to present my traditional 
comedic story-telling.

00:19:09.750 --> 00:19:12.750
Polar 
Bear's 
Café

00:19:09.750 --> 00:19:12.750
Pentei 
Ginta

00:19:13.540 --> 00:19:15.710
Five, six, seven...

00:19:15.710 --> 00:19:19.950
How many herrings were in that soba?

00:19:19.950 --> 00:19:21.550
There were four.

00:19:22.030 --> 00:19:27.440
Five, six, seven, eight, nine...

00:19:28.640 --> 00:19:30.770
And that's it for me.

00:19:33.600 --> 00:19:35.480
Thank you!

00:19:36.290 --> 00:19:38.900
That's the first time I was able 
to finish the whole thing!

00:19:39.300 --> 00:19:41.750
It was wonderful.

00:19:42.610 --> 00:19:44.490
Let me get a set of those cards.

00:19:44.490 --> 00:19:46.230
R-Really?

00:19:46.230 --> 00:19:47.230
Of course.

00:19:47.230 --> 00:19:48.910
Thank you very much.

00:19:49.410 --> 00:19:51.000
I'll take a set, too.

00:19:51.960 --> 00:19:54.030
Thank you very much.

00:19:54.720 --> 00:19:55.910
Hey, Penguin.

00:19:56.380 --> 00:19:58.100
Let's have an encore.

00:19:58.100 --> 00:20:01.120
Really?! Thank you very much.

00:20:04.780 --> 00:20:06.670
I opened up a bottle of champagne.

00:20:07.570 --> 00:20:08.770
How about we have some?

00:20:09.160 --> 00:20:10.370
Sounds good.

00:20:10.860 --> 00:20:14.000
Oh good. You're all still here.

00:20:14.000 --> 00:20:16.970
Hey, Wolf. Glad you could make it.

00:20:18.100 --> 00:20:19.290
Want some?

00:20:19.870 --> 00:20:22.280
I got one from the shop.

00:20:22.660 --> 00:20:28.240
It's hard to tell if you're 
a baker, a wolf, or Santa.

00:20:28.620 --> 00:20:30.660
Really? You're gonna be the 
one to bring that up?

00:20:30.660 --> 00:20:34.170
Polar 
Bear's 
Café

00:20:34.590 --> 00:20:36.380
All right, let's eat.

00:20:37.010 --> 00:20:38.340
I'll cut it into seven pieces.

00:20:39.380 --> 00:20:40.260
Good evening.

00:20:43.890 --> 00:20:45.260
Eight pieces it is.

00:20:45.260 --> 00:20:47.760
Panda

00:20:51.740 --> 00:20:53.050
Come on now.

00:20:53.050 --> 00:20:55.700
You need to take off the pochette 
when you're eating at least.

00:20:57.950 --> 00:20:59.950
Isn't it great?

00:21:00.440 --> 00:21:01.270
Goodness.

00:21:01.640 --> 00:21:03.810
I'll make an exception 
because it's Christmas.

00:21:04.320 --> 00:21:08.200
I wonder if he'll like 
my present, too.

00:21:16.530 --> 00:21:18.290
That was delicious.

00:21:18.820 --> 00:21:20.220
It'll be great if we can go

00:21:20.220 --> 00:21:23.020
again next year and the 
year after that, too.

00:21:23.020 --> 00:21:23.550
Yes.

00:21:33.310 --> 00:21:35.640
To Prince Han

00:21:34.260 --> 00:21:35.640
Prince Han?

00:21:47.840 --> 00:21:50.430
This is the first time

00:21:50.430 --> 00:21:52.200
I've had such a fun Christmas!

00:21:52.620 --> 00:21:54.870
Totally got the Adélie penguin card!

00:21:55.360 --> 00:21:58.610
Let's open another 
champagne! One more!

00:22:00.060 --> 00:22:02.050
Then let's open an extra special one.

00:22:02.610 --> 00:22:04.020
We're totally gonna open it.

00:22:04.580 --> 00:22:06.010
All right!

00:22:06.010 --> 00:22:07.610
Let me have some, too!

00:22:07.610 --> 00:22:09.450
Could I have some, as well?

00:22:09.450 --> 00:22:11.120
Shall we toast, then?

00:22:11.120 --> 00:22:13.040
Could we get some, too?

00:22:13.040 --> 00:22:14.250
Thank you.

00:22:14.250 --> 00:22:16.020
Thank you!

00:22:16.020 --> 00:22:17.450
All right, then...

00:22:18.090 --> 00:22:20.260
Merry Christmas!

00:23:54.950 --> 00:24:24.960
Next Time

00:23:58.000 --> 00:23:59.660
Mr. Penguin, Mr. Penguin.

00:23:59.660 --> 00:24:00.670
You've finally appeared!

00:24:00.670 --> 00:24:01.940
What is it, Miss Sasako?

00:24:01.940 --> 00:24:04.670
Please don't mind me 
and continue talking.

00:24:04.670 --> 00:24:05.990
Hey, Mr. Penguin.

00:24:05.990 --> 00:24:07.960
Don't you get a delicious taste in

00:24:07.960 --> 00:24:09.760
your mouth when you say "Panda"?

00:24:09.760 --> 00:24:11.010
Could I not answer that?

00:24:11.010 --> 00:24:11.880
Panda.

00:24:11.880 --> 00:24:13.420
I don't think you really 
needed to try it out.

00:24:13.420 --> 00:24:15.090
Now we've got another troublemaker.

00:24:15.090 --> 00:24:16.510
Let's end this, Polar Bear.

00:24:16.510 --> 00:24:18.220
Next week's Polar Bear's Café

00:24:18.220 --> 00:24:19.980
will have seven mistakes.

00:24:19.980 --> 00:24:20.850
What are they?

00:24:20.850 --> 00:24:23.080
There won't be any, 
so please don't look for them.

00:24:22.250 --> 00:24:25.260
Big Cleaning at the Café
For Whom Does the Bell Toll?

00:24:23.080 --> 00:24:24.120
Good luck!
